//RS // `--port=<N>`/`--target=web` CLI flags. Std-only (I6): `TcpListener`, manual
//RS // HTTP/1.1 parsing, mtime-poll watch, `std::process::Command` to shell out to
//RS // the real `jet` binary for each rebuild. This file is compiled INTO the
//RS // standalone native binary produced for `fn dev()` — it never links against
//RS // jet-parser/jet-sema/jet-codegen/jet-driver, so a rebuild always goes through
//RS // `jet build --target=web <file>` as a subprocess, mirroring the design of
//RS // Source/CmdDevWeb.rs's `run_dev_web` (mtime-poll watch, atomic staged
//RS // rebuild, polling live-reload) without literally calling its internal
//RS // functions.
